# ── Secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The assistant's API key lives in .env.local. It must never be committed:
# anything that reaches a public repo is public forever, even if the file
# is deleted in a later commit.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
dist/
node_modules/
.vercel/

# ── Generated assets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A note on why most of this IS committed.
#
# public/img, public/media and public/doc are produced by `npm run
# assets` and `npm run audio`, which need Python, Pillow, pypdfium2 and
# ffmpeg. The deploy only runs `npm run build`, which is Node. If these
# were ignored the built site would come out with no portrait, no
# project figures, no music and no CV — and nothing would report an
# error, because as far as the build is concerned nothing is missing.
#
# So they are committed, and the host needs nothing but Node.
#
# public/data is the one exception: `npm run build` regenerates it
# before Vite runs, so it is always fresh in the output.
public/data/

# Staging for the audio encoder; public/media/about holds the published
# copies, which are the ones that ship.
about/web/

# ── Masters ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The uncompressed audio and the raw video are large and are only inputs.
about/*.wav
images/projects/**/*.mp4

# ── Editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/

# ── Raw coursework ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The university folders these projects were written up from. Nothing
# reads them: the pipeline's inputs are images/, about/ and cv/, and the
# write-ups themselves live in src/lib/work/. They are ~52 MB of source
# material that the site does not need in order to build, so they stay
# on your machine rather than in every clone.
computer vision projects/
control systems projects/
fpga projects/
machine learning projects/
